WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.340
Candlelight.

2
00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:05.100
Lady Macbeth learns that King
Duncan will stay the night.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.590
Alone, she calls into the
dark: "Come, you spirits".

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:15.480
She begs them to "unsex me here",
and fill her with "direst cruelty".

5
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:16.780
Act 5.

6
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.260
The same woman walks the castle at night,

7
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:22.190
carrying a taper, rubbing her hands.

8
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.590
She begged to be made pitiless.

9
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.080
So why is she the first to crack?

10
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:30.570
In this mission, you'll take
her speech to the spirits apart,

11
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.110
word by word.

12
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.290
You'll see how the play ties
courage, and even cruelty,

13
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.730
to being a man.

14
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:41.330
And you'll follow her, scene by
scene, all the way to that night walk.

15
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.820
Your mission: explain
why she cracks first.
